# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules. Order matters: first match wins.
# Old WordPress asset paths must 404 rather than resolve to anything.
/wp-content/*   /404.html   404
/wp-includes/*  /404.html   404
/wp-admin/*     /404.html   404
/wp-json/*      /404.html   404
/xmlrpc.php     /404.html   404

# Trailing-slash URLs are canonical on this site, matching the old WordPress
# paths exactly, so nothing needs rewriting here. If the client's redirect
# table is exported later, its 301s go below this line.

# From the Rank Math export (2026-09-08): the redirections table is EMPTY, so
# there are no custom 301s to carry over. Every old URL path is reproduced
# verbatim by this site, so nothing needs forwarding.
#
# One live behaviour NOT reproduced: Rank Math had attachment_redirect_urls=on,
# sending WordPress attachment pages to https://gositeflyer.com with a 301.
# No attachment URLs appear in the sitemap, so none are indexed, and there is no
# stable pattern to match statically. If any turn up in Search Console later,
# add them here.
